MID_EV10_100_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV10_100_m01_024: ...
MID_EV10_100_m01_001: The wheels of fate have begun to turn.
MID_EV10_100_m01_002: For now, we'll watch at a remove to ensure\neverything goes as it should.
MID_EV10_100_m01_003: Though we may need to take an active hand if any\nserious trouble arises.
MID_EV10_100_m01_004: <NCA>"Will they be alright?"
MID_EV10_100_m01_005: <NCB>"I don't like this."
MID_EV10_100_m01_006: <ACA>Naturally. Else we have failed in our task.
MID_EV10_100_m01_007: <ACA>If left unchanged, the flow of their causality would\nlead them to ruin. Happily, we are here to prevent it.
MID_EV10_100_m01_008: <ACB>There are limits to what we may influence.
MID_EV10_100_m01_009: <ACB>Or did you mean you would rather observe from\na nearer distance?
MID_EV10_100_m01_010: I suppose 'tis true that we can do little to intervene\nfrom here.
MID_EV10_100_m01_011: But you must understand that it cannot be any\nother way.
MID_EV10_100_m01_012: The work of tampering with causality is delicate.
MID_EV10_100_m01_014: Our forms here are mere hollow vessels and have\nthe power only to make slight ripples in the flow.
MID_EV10_100_m01_015: To manifest physically over and over would quickly\nexpend my precious strength.
MID_EV10_100_m01_016: I'd rather keep that power in reserve until we've\nseen them to where they're going.
MID_EV10_100_m01_017: Mm...
MID_EV10_100_m01_018: Your pleading won't change anything. Though here's\na thought...
MID_EV10_100_m01_019: Providing you with the form of a small bird would\nnot overtax my strength.
MID_EV10_100_m01_020: You could then at least offer some small advice.
MID_EV10_100_m01_021: If that's acceptable to you, then take the form of a\nbird, and find perches to await them.
MID_EV10_100_m01_022: Perhaps they'll take a moment to contact you as\nthey pass.
MID_EV10_100_m01_023: Put your faith in your connection with them, and\ntrust that they shall seek you out.
MID_EV10_001_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV10_001_m01_001: 'Twas a near thing, but they seem to have made it\nout unscathed.
MID_EV10_001_m01_019: Whew...
MID_EV10_001_m01_004: I must say, you put up a fine showing against\nthe thing.
MID_EV10_001_m01_005: Small wonder, given that she selected you personally\nfor this task.
MID_EV10_001_m01_006: Though what you faced was merely Balor's shade.\nIt paled in comparison to the real thing.
MID_EV10_001_m01_007: <NCA>"That wasn't really him?"
MID_EV10_001_m01_008: <NCB>"He didn't seem like much."
MID_EV10_001_m01_009: <ACA>It depends on one's perspective. The thing you\nfought was like a sliver of Balor's mind.
MID_EV10_001_m01_010: <ACA>His fierce hatred tends to congeal in the underworld,\nhis domain, like a sort of sediment.
MID_EV10_001_m01_011: <ACA>'Tis unusual for it to take human shape and lash out\nso. Though that is the simplified explanation.
MID_EV10_001_m01_012: <ACB>A bold claim! I look forward to seeing you back it up.
MID_EV10_001_m01_013: <ACB>If only he were so meager in the flesh, I could make\nshort work of him myself.
MID_EV10_001_m01_014: I was surprised to see the underworld invade\nour world as it did.
MID_EV10_001_m01_015: The proximity of the underworld made it a bit easier\nto manifest where we needed to be.
MID_EV10_001_m01_016: 'Twas lucky for us, but I still used up a bit more\npower than I'd prefer.
MID_EV10_001_m01_018: I'd advise against being so reckless again. Our\nresources are not infinite.
MID_EV10_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV10_002_m01_023: Hm...
MID_EV10_002_m01_001: 'Twas certainly a shock that the Demonic Beast\ncalled Cetus was once a human.
MID_EV10_002_m01_002: That must be why something felt off about it...\nIts nature was different from me and my siblings.
MID_EV10_002_m01_003: <NCA>"What exactly is that blade?"
MID_EV10_002_m01_004: <NCB>"How did a person become a Demonic Beast?"
MID_EV10_002_m01_005: <ACA>The weapon he bears? As I recall, they referred to it\nas a Hero's Relic.
MID_EV10_002_m01_006: <ACA>One of the weapons crafted from the heart and bones\nof my siblings. 'Tis repulsive.
MID_EV10_002_m01_007: <ACB>The process is opaque to me, but our hearts hold\npower in them even after our bodies fall to ruin.
MID_EV10_002_m01_008: <ACB>At a guess, some outside factor causes the power\nwithin to lose control. More than that, I can't say.
MID_EV10_002_m01_009: I wonder what sorts of things are happening in the\nland of Fódlan...
MID_EV10_002_m01_010: But I'll set that curiosity aside while we focus on\nthe mission set to us.
MID_EV10_002_m01_012: I must say, the matter of Cetus is only one thing\nthat troubles me.
MID_EV10_002_m01_013: Why does that man seek out battle so relentlessly?\nI find him confounding.
MID_EV10_002_m01_017: <NCA>"We'll need him."
MID_EV10_002_m01_018: I can't deny it. His skill as a warrior is peerless.
MID_EV10_002_m01_019: Having him as an ally would bolster our chances,\nbut...I wish I liked him more.
MID_EV10_002_m01_020: Yet there is no mistaking him as one of those whom\nI found adrift in the sea of causality.
MID_EV10_002_m01_021: Very well, then. Let us continue to observe him.
MID_EV10_003_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV10_003_m01_021: Huh...
MID_EV10_003_m01_001: Hrm. A man-made trinket to manipulate the\nmind, eh?
MID_EV10_003_m01_002: That's all very well for now, but I wonder...
MID_EV10_003_m01_003: <NCA>"What's the matter?"
MID_EV10_003_m01_004: <NCB>"You're overthinking it."
MID_EV10_003_m01_005: <ACA>I can't bring myself to believe that everything will\ngo smoothly from this point on.
MID_EV10_003_m01_006: <ACA>Don't you agree there are too many risks in play?
MID_EV10_003_m01_007: <ACB>I would love nothing more than to believe that all\nwill be well.
MID_EV10_003_m01_008: <ACB>But the forces involved here are too powerful to\ndiscount. Do you disagree?
MID_EV10_003_m01_009: I'll grant that I don't know the limits of what that\nchain is capable of.
MID_EV10_003_m01_010: But that right arm—all the remains, really—is a\nconduit for the residual malice within.
MID_EV10_003_m01_011: That malice won't be contained by any\nsimple means.
MID_EV10_003_m01_012: Not when it derives from that abomination...
MID_EV10_003_m01_014: But more than that, this whole situation feels\nstrangely unsettled.
MID_EV10_003_m01_015: I fear the worst is not yet over for her.
MID_EV10_003_m01_016: Violent storms lurk ahead in Theodora's causality.
MID_EV10_003_m01_017: <NCA>"I'm sure she'll be fine."
MID_EV10_003_m01_018: Hmph...I suppose so. That is our purpose here.
MID_EV10_003_m01_019: We are to watch over her and ensure that she is\nguided toward a desirable causality.
MID_EV10_003_m01_020: Keep your eye on her and don't lower your guard.\nMuch depends on it.
MID_EV10_004_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV10_004_m01_023: Mm...
MID_EV10_004_m01_001: So...she doesn't balk at destroying herself in order to\nexact her revenge.
MID_EV10_004_m01_002: I don't see why one so young would willingly walk\nthis trail of carnage.
MID_EV10_004_m01_003: <NCA>"Are you worried for her?"
MID_EV10_004_m01_004: <NCB>"You sound unusually concerned."
MID_EV10_004_m01_005: <ACA>Hmm... Not in so many words.
MID_EV10_004_m01_006: <ACA>But when we first touched upon this girl's causality,\nshe was still a child.
MID_EV10_004_m01_007: <ACA>I may still be sentimental about the look in her eyes\nfrom those days.
MID_EV10_004_m01_008: <ACB>I can't help but think that this Leda girl is lying\nto herself.
MID_EV10_004_m01_009: <ACB>She claims not to care if she dies, but I have the\nfeeling that isn't the truth.
MID_EV10_004_m01_010: <ACB>It's as though she's kept up this facade for so long\nthat even she is fooled. Though I could be wrong.
MID_EV10_004_m01_012: <NCA>"You've changed a little."
MID_EV10_004_m01_013: 'Tis poor manners to speak as if you know me so.
MID_EV10_004_m01_014: A trace amount of godly blood does run in her veins.
MID_EV10_004_m01_015: But 'tis astonishing that she can use its full power\nwhile keeping her mind intact.
MID_EV10_004_m01_016: Perhaps she really is favored by Balor.
MID_EV10_004_m01_024: Ah...
MID_EV10_004_m01_019: I've had a foreboding feeling about her for some\ntime now.
MID_EV10_004_m01_021: She may be about to delve into something much\nbigger than her.
MID_EV10_004_m01_022: If so, she could soon need our help. Let's remain\nvigilant, just in case.
